Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, an if-then statement provides a way to “test” a condition, and if it is true, do one thing, and if it is false, do another thing.  Here is a basic example:

int main()
{
   int x = 0;

   if (x > 0)
   {
      System.out.println("x is positive");
   }
   else
   {
      System.out.println("x is not positive");
   }
   return 0;
}
